dropped the body
--
N5008 [dcl.init.string]/1: `const wchar_t w[] = L"de";' -- an array of
character type initialized from a string literal of the matching kind takes
its bound from the literal.  The C++ front end handled narrow literals only;
wide/UTF literals (already array expressions) fell to the generic conversion
and were rejected ("invalid implicit conversion from 'int [3l]' to 'const int
[]'").
